Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/50] Crime: off at server start; /crime on and /crime off
 switch it

Renn's crime rules, CONCORD, faction police and navy, sentry guns and
logoff timers start switched on.  They now start off
(<crime><Enabled>false</Enabled> and the code default), so new things
can be tested anywhere in peace.

/crime on turns them on while the server runs: systems already loaded
get their gate and station sentry guns, as a system booted with crime
on does, and pilots already in space are checked for the faction
police and navy as if they had just arrived.

/crime off clears every flag and timer (aggression, criminal, weapons
and logoff timers, illegal aggressors, sentry and NPC aggression) and
tells the clients, so the overview and the neocom countdown clear.
Every CONCORD, police and navy response leaves with its tackle, jams
and cloak block; the sentry guns are taken out of space and their
items deleted; and ships left in space by pilots who logged off leave
space at once, saved where their pilots logged off.  Kill rights are
kept.

/crime with no arguments says which it is.  The test crime,
/crime (me|charID|entityID) [victimID], says to turn crime on first
while it is off.  With crime off, taking from another pilot's can or
wreck no longer brings up the client's theft warning.
